&lt;p&gt;If you’re brand new to Adobe Experience Manager (AEM), one of the first things you’ll hear about is something called the &lt;strong&gt;JCR&lt;/strong&gt;—short for &lt;strong&gt;Java Content Repository&lt;/strong&gt;. That might sound intimidating, especially if you don’t have a Java background (I didn’t either), but don’t worry. This post is here to give you a simple, high-level mental model.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>